  "$comment": "What each app decides from an OpenBot's deployment answer (shared/client-version.ts `compatibility`). The web app, the Recorder, OpenBot Desktop and OpenBot Mobile each run every case. `deployments` are real answers: `current` is what this release's server answers with no admin raise (no built-in minimum: a server serves every app released in the last 12 months, and no OpenBot release is older than that yet), `v1.1.0` is what OpenBot 1.1.0 answers (no version fields; captured from a running v1.1.0 server), `raised` is this release with an admin's OPENBOT_MINIMUM_CLIENTS=desktop=1.2.0,mobile=1.2.0,recorder=1.2.0,web=1.1.0 (an admin can't raise the web app above the server's own release, whose pages it serves), `next` is a 1.2.0 server whose admin raised every app to 1.2.0, as a tab left open across that upgrade meets it,, `security` is this release with every app but the web app raised to 1.2.0 because of a security problem in older releases (`securityMinimumClients` names the same minimums), and `v3-only` is a later OpenBot that serves only a new API. A case with `security` true expects the app's decision to say the minimum is there for security.",
